1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
The part stays fixed. The agent changes the machining plan.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Checks → stock-removal simulation → timing judge → CAM feedback.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Actual indexed machining replay, driven by the submitted movements.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The table reorients between cuts. Stock is removed along cutter sweeps.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Three new complex parts: 75.8 → 20.8 estimated minutes.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
72.5% below reference. The carrier improved another 6.4% after judge feedback.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
This staggered drum uses 17 indexed orientations and 26 features.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The drum’s next proposal was slower. The loop kept its earlier passing plan.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The manifold reference fails. Astra receives the diagnosis and revises CAM.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The repair passes. A saved exact-match check catches repeated failures.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Weave scores retained records: geometry gates and machining-time metrics.

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
ARIA suggested an experiment. We ran 12 cases and scoped its advice.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
24 fresh plans across four parts: memory transfer is mixed.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,000
New geometries show no useful general speed benefit from memory.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Three chambers, cross-ports and registers: actual manifold cutter movements.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Recorded fresh PDF job: reviewed drawing → CAM → checks → simulation.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
These are actual saved events and artifacts. Waiting time is compressed.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Timing feedback and memory are retained for inspection and later proposals.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,900
Prototype: indexed 3+2, 1 mm cells, 3 mm tolerance. Not production verification.

